<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Amway Asia upped.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Amway Asia upped.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- J.P. Morgan analysts Michael Grant and Gregory Boosin on Thursday raised their rating for Amway Asia Pacific Ltd to buy from long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- The upgrade was &quot;based on China's greater level of contribution and growth seen in the second quarter, reported March 26,&quot; they wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;... We are increasing our fiscal year estimates to $1.87 and $2.20 for August 1997 and 1998, respectively, (from $1.77 and $2.07).&quot;</p>
<p>-- Shares in the company opened up 1/4 at 41-1/2 on Thursday.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
